# 6. Standard Mathematical and Scientific Techniques

AkbasCore uses established mathematical and computational techniques as
building blocks.

No claim of original invention is made here over standard techniques such as:

- vector normalization;
- cosine similarity;
- difference-of-means construction;
- covariance estimation;
- singular value decomposition (SVD);
- low-rank approximation;
- regularization;
- orthogonal projection;
- Fisher/LDA-style geometry;
- principal-component analysis;
- bootstrap estimation;
- gradient-based optimization;
- standard transformer hidden-state extraction.

These techniques retain their ordinary mathematical and scientific provenance.

The AkbasCore research record concerns the documented architecture,
experimental construction, integration, measurements, terminology and
versioned implementations of the project.

